00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.270 align:start position:0%
 
i want to thank nabb for this  opportunity to address you at the annual  meetings  are you passionate about plant breeding  i want to begin today by acknowledging  dr anne marie throw  the first napb friend of plant breeding  i found these quotes from anne marie in  an article honoring anne-marie's life of  service  it was posted online in december 2016  prior to her being selected for the  first friends of plant breeding award in  2017  i'm sure anne marie did not anticipate  her words would be shared here today  but they are perfect  as a model that she has set for us as  friends of plant breeding  anne marie said  i enjoy the role of taking the  initiative to look around  to see things that need to be done  and get started  often others join in and carry on the  work  anne-marie is passionate about plant  breeding  this is the role model for all napb  friends of plant breeding that is being  amplified here today for our emerging  plant breeders  look around  see the need  get started  others will join carry on the work  don't wait to get involved this approach  is great for all plant breeders and in  the pb members  it is a lesson that has been enshrined  in the career and legacy of dr norman  borlaug  he was another visionary plant breeder  and a doer he had a deep sense of  urgency compelling him to action  he had a passion for plant breeding  like anne marie dr borlaug passed on  that passion to others at every  opportunity he especially enjoyed  inspiring and encouraging emerging plant  breeders and hunger fighters  he counted on others to join in and  carry on the work  reflecting on her career anne marie said  i am grateful to have been able to bring  different researchers together into  networks and projects  this benefits science and the public by  creating opportunities to exchange good  ideas recruit young scientists and  search for funding  that is where i can help  as someone who understands the world of  science  seeks to be useful and enjoys creating  connections and  looking for opportunities  i think anne-marie's words  could have been written by dr borlaug  it is the same spirit the same passion  for plant breeding and for making the  world a better place  as a friend of plant breeding i share  anne-marie's views  i enjoy being useful  creating connections building  relationships looking for opportunities  to serve  the community  and acting on those visions  i love encouraging others to join in  and carry on the work i find they often  improve  what is being started  napb owes much gratitude to anne marie's  vision and hard work to help bring us  together as the national association of  plant breeders  i think anne marie would agree  that this is a wonderful feeling to be  recognized by your friends and  colleagues for having and sharing this  passion  for plant breeding  it is a great honor to be in the same  short list with anne marie  as a friend of plant breeding  plant-breeding passion  what is it  why is it important and where does it  come from  here are some statements about passion  for you to ponder  i love the word ponder i don't think we  do enough of it  passion is a strong desire that can get  you to do amazing things  passion can push you through difficult  times  because you don't care what it takes to  become better  passion is an emotion to be acted upon  without action passion yields no  worthwhile result  when you have passion for something you  love it even when you hate it  i'm not sure i know what that one means  i'll let you ponder that for yourself  finally  you can have all the passion in the  world for something but if you never do  anything about it  that passion  is useless  how do we relate plant breeding and  passion  what is plant breeding passion  plant breeding passion is a strong  desire to achieve results through new  cultivars  a thirst to be relevant  our cultivars must have impact  plant-breeding passion increases by  seeing the success of hybrids and  varieties that you helped to become  viable products  ones that have real impact and many  lives across the landscape  i like that we have an award two awards  now  recognizing noteworthy impact of plant  breeding  such awards show non-plant breeders the  importance of what we do  they demonstrate what exceptional plant  breeding passion looks like  for me plant-breeding passion includes  a sense of urgency  speed breeding shuttle breeding cycle  time genomic and phenomic selection  prediction  gene editing etc  it's sometimes described as fire in the  belly  indicating that it comes from deep  within  a strong work ethic  gitterton attitude  i can tell you plant breeding passion is  important because employers value it  hiring managers evaluated  selection committees discuss it prior to  the final hiring  i base this on my experience working  with many hiring managers and teams at  monsanto as global breeder sourcing lead  around the world they all wanted  candidates to show that they were  passionate about the breeding roles that  they were applying to  it is one of those intangibles  that can make the difference on who gets  the job offer  i think it's important because it  instills hope  in others who are working to solve  complex challenges where  improved plants can help us  i could not have been a successful plant  breeder without hope feeding my passion  teams function better  more gets done in less  time innovation is stimulated  success breeds success  plant breeding passion is highly  contagious  when nourished properly it encourages  others  breeders who have it  love what they do every day  plant-breeding passion typically comes  from experienced and influential people  people you trust  caring people  think about influential people like  beloved mentors who instilled the desire  for plant breeding in you  often  when meeting graduate students for the  first time i ask them  how did you become interested in plant  breeding  there was almost always an experienced  mentor  or influential person that made the big  difference  for them in choosing our profession  and pouring themselves into it so i like  to think relationships  are the soil  and encouragement is the fertilizer for  growing passion in plant breeders  initially it comes from others  think of your mentors  it gets internalized  and comes from it within  this does not happen overnight  external factors can shape it  population growth wars poverty and  starvation  and climate change  these drivers can have an impact  but i think  they are usually secondary to the  relationships that lead the way  like plants our passion in plant  breeding grows stronger over time  mentorship and awards programs change  lives  shown here in may of night of 2014  is a mentorship program known as the  hayes phillips lectureship and graduate  student award it was created 40 years  prior in 1974  through the vision of dr ron phillips at  the university of minnesota  i believe 2021 was the 48th year for  this program  perhaps some of you have benefited from  it  the longevity and success of the program  testifies to its success i can tell you  confidently that without this program  there likely would not be a borlaug  scholars travel grant  and mentoring program in napb today  ron phillips was not my advisor he was  not my on my graduate committee  he was however a trusted mentor in the  lab next door to the one i worked in he  cared about students i benefited from  that fact  in 1976 i received the third h k hayes  award  that year dr phillips invited  distinguished  alumnus dr norman borlaug  to be the invited speaker for this award  ceremony he also invited dr wayne kyme  i proudly include dr keim here because  without this purdue professor taking  interest in students i would not have  had a plant breeding career  you see  i had been admitted to dental school but  dr kyme made me a better offer  a career path in applied plant genetics  and plant breeding  i love dentists but it was an easy  choice for me i love plant breeding more  all of this brings me to the point  although i experienced a wonderful  career in private sector breeding corn  i never forgot the importance of public  plant breeders who encouraged and  enabled this career path  i didn't know this career existed  now back to my story  prior to the event dr phillips handed me  this copy of a book entitled campaigns  against hunger published in 1967.  three years prior to when dr borlaug  received the 1970 nobel peace prize  i graduated from high school in 1967 i  could relate to this book  dr phillips said i had to read it prior  to dr borlaug's arrival  he sent me to the pathology department  to meet with dr e c statement an  emeritus  professor  who was an author and editor dr stakeman  signed my book  ron prophetically told me that the book  would mean more to me later in life  he was right  in night in  2007 i had dr borlaug  signed the book just below dr stakeman's  signature  dr borlaug's granddaughter julie told me  that it was an emotional experience  bringing back a flood of memories for dr  borlaug seeing his mentor's signature  after more than 30 years  this mentoring program created by dr  phillips  accelerated the growing plant-breeding  passion within me  it was the encouragement i needed at the  right time  i love the picture on the back cover of  this book jacket  it depicts the three authors in front of  their vehicle  that they drove on their original 1941  tour of  mexican agriculture to determine whether  the u.s could impact food production  there  that survey trip ultimately ended up  being a spark that ignited the green  revolution what i love about it is that  the picture included one incredibly  lucky graduate student richard schulte's  who was invited along by professor  mangelsdorf  it intrigues me to imagine his version  of that historic trip  graduate students have a unique  perspective that i really value when  working on projects with them  on the right is a picture of this book  meaning more to me later in life while  using it to mentor the inaugural group  of the 2018  napb borlaug scholars with their mentors  you see as a friend of plant breeding i  understand the importance of plant  breeding passion  i know that most if not all of you  listening share the same passion for our  profession and our scientific craft  like ann marie you should look around  see things that need to be done and get  started  like her you should expect others to  join in and carry on the work  remember  you can have all the passion in the  world for something but if you never do  anything about it that patient passion  is useless  i will end with this  napb is a wonderful organization for  turning plant breeding passion into  actions  i make this statement because napb has  so many incredibly talented members  who are already deeply passionate about  plant breeding  we are doing great things we are doing  the right things  we can and should do more of the right  things  we are still a young organization we are  still growing in my opinion we're  growing too slowly  where is the sense of urgency where's  the fire in the belly the passion  in july of 2019 napb had  451 total members  in our strategic plan we set an  achievable goal of reaching 650 members  by 2023  that would have required gaining 40  members per year over the next five  years  we needed this level of growth to  support our grand goal of hiring our  first dedicated staff person  in july of 2021 we had 477  members  that is a net gain of 26 members in 24  months  surely we can do better than one new  member a month  now we need to make up for lost time  therefore i have an urgent challenge  for each one of you regarding 2022 napb  membership  hear me now  write this down  please set a personal goal of recruiting  at least one new napb member  who does not appear in our current  member directory  as any pb members you all have access to  our online directory  you can type in any name to see whether  your potential recruit is an active  member  this is a great opportunity to increase  our membership diversity  do not quit on this goal until you are  successful  this is key to napb growth in 2022  when that name of your recruit shows up  in our directory you can declare success  it is an easily attainable and  measurable goal  this is key to napb growth in 2022 and  beyond  make it a reoccurring annual goal  as you renew your membership annually  look around find a committee  and volunteer your services  please support our grand goal for hiring  our first napb staff member by 2023  your contributions to the napb general  fund will help drive this goal  now i would like to acknowledge and  personally thank our passionate four lug  scholars  for a successful fundraising  campaign this year  it was their idea and their effort thank  you  thank you to our generous borlaug  scholars donors and faithful sponsors  you are nurturing plant breeding passion  in a very direct way  i commend you all for your voluntary  actions and selfless service to napb  driven by your passion for plant  breeding you are all friends of plant  breeding  express your passion  with action  get her done  it's a great time to be a plant breeder

